#THIS IS FILE IMP72MAIN, THE C MAIN OF AN IMP72 PROGRAM, IN IMP (IT WAS C, LIB/IMP72MAIN.C): THE MAIN PROGRAM OF THE SOURCE (THE STATEMENTS BEFORE ITS FIRST SUBR) IS THE FUNCTION IMPMAIN.  IT IS IN A LIBRARY MEMBER
 OF ITS OWN SO THAT A PROGRAM WITH A MAIN OF ITS OWN DOES NOT LINK THIS ONE.  THE COMMAND LINE IS KEPT FOR THE PROGRAM TO ASK FOR WITH CCALL: IMPARGC(0) AND IMPARGVP(0) FOR THE ARRAY.
 THE C LIBRARY CALLS MAIN WITH ARGC AND ARGV BY VALUE; AN IMP ROUTINE TAKES ITS ARGUMENTS BY REFERENCE, SO THE VALUES ARE THE ADDRESSES IT IS GIVEN: LOC(ARGC) IS ARGC (THE LOW 32 BITS OF IT: THE REST OF THE
 REGISTER IS NOT DEFINED) AND LOC(ARGV) IS ARGV #
IMPACV,IMPAVV ARE COMMON;
SUBR IMPARGC(Z) IS IMPACV;
SUBR IMPARGVP(Z) IS IMPAVV;
SUBR MAIN(ARGC,ARGV) IS (
 IMPACV:=LOC(ARGC) AND 4294967295;
 IMPAVV:=LOC(ARGV);
 IMPMAIN(0);
 0)
%%
